    "body": "Problem: When `MCursor` is linked to `Cursor` it is not easy to distinguish the main and extra cursors. Although this is rarely needed when editing (since edit is applied at all of them), it is fairly needed when jumping between the cursors with `[C` / `]C`. Plus different highlighting for main and extra cursor looks (subjectively) more pleasent.\r\n\r\nSolution: Link `MCursor` by default to `CurSearch`. Linking to an existing group (instead of forcing fixed default attributes) makes the highlighting more readily useful for user color schemes.\r\n\r\nThe `CurSearch` is chosen because:\r\n\r\n1. It is semantically close as \"something at cursor\". This also means that it is not meant to be used for something not at cursor, so highlighting for extra cursors should rarely be confused with something else.\r\n\r\n2. It is meant to be visible, usually via visible background. This is also valuable for showing cursors, as it plays nicely when this group is used for coloring extra cursor in Kitty multiple-cursors protocol: cursors in Insert mode are usually thin vertical bars which require a visible color.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHere is a demo of how this looks in a Kitty with extra cursor highlighted with `MCursor` background and foreground:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf8dc3fc-aed1-43de-9d25-ed6c3c3b2e9c\r\n\r\nThe `init.lua` used for demo (a modified version of #41603):\r\n\r\n<details><summary>MCursor in Kitty protocol</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal get_fg_bg = function(name)\r\n  local hl = vim.api.nvim_get_hl(0, { name = name, link = false })\r\n  local fg = hl.reverse and hl.bg or hl.fg\r\n  local bg = hl.reverse and hl.fg or hl.bg\r\n  return { fg = fg, bg = bg }\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal set_mcursor_attr = function(which, dec)\r\n  if dec == nil then return end\r\n  local b = math.fmod(dec, 256)\r\n  local g = math.fmod((dec - b) / 256, 256)\r\n  local r = math.floor(dec / 65536)\r\n  vim.api.nvim_ui_send(string.format('\\027[>%s;2:%s:%s:%s q', which, r, g, b))\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'UIEnter', 'ColorScheme' }, {\r\n  callback = function()\r\n    local hl_mcursor = get_fg_bg('MCursor')\r\n    local hl_normal = get_fg_bg('Normal')\r\n    set_mcursor_attr('30', hl_mcursor.fg or hl_normal.fg)\r\n    set_mcursor_attr('40', hl_mcursor.bg or hl_normal.bg)\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('VimLeave', {\r\n  callback = function() vim.api.nvim_ui_send('\\027[>30;0;40;0 q') end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>",
